{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01145",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.64,
      "end_seconds": 2.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Evening. Let's get started."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.67,
      "end_seconds": 7.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Okay, so good morning, doctor, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.85,
      "end_seconds": 12.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.22,
      "end_seconds": 23.92,
      "duration_seconds": 9.7,
      "text": "Oh, uh, honestly, it's swelling around the ankle, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.71,
      "end_seconds": 28.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.43,
      "end_seconds": 33.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "It's been going on for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.3,
      "end_seconds": 43.82,
      "duration_seconds": 8.52,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.49,
      "end_seconds": 49.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "Mild, really. Only raising it, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.58,
      "end_seconds": 54.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.93,
      "end_seconds": 69.05,
      "duration_seconds": 13.12,
      "text": "So, you know, it usually comes with bruising. Oh, and there's a feeling of the ankle giving way as well, about two weeks now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 82.6,
      "end_seconds": 90.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Heart rate 80, SpO2 99 percent on room air, blood pressure 120 over 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.2,
      "end_seconds": 92.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.12,
      "end_seconds": 99.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.57,
      "end_seconds": 101.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.37,
      "end_seconds": 120.55,
      "duration_seconds": 9.18,
      "text": "There is swelling and bruising over the outer ankle and I can't find any bony tenderness at the back of the ankle bone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.59,
      "end_seconds": 123.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.33,
      "end_seconds": 133.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. And what about calf pain, previous fracture or knee pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.47,
      "end_seconds": 139.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "No, no calf pain, previous fracture or knee pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.71,
      "end_seconds": 150.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "Did you get cracking sound at the time or pain at the base of the fifth toe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.52,
      "end_seconds": 155.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Okay, so no, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.39,
      "end_seconds": 162.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.35,
      "end_seconds": 167.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Well, no, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.65,
      "end_seconds": 172.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "So, is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.23,
      "end_seconds": 176.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "My daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.33,
      "end_seconds": 196.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.33,
      "end_seconds": 201.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Wheat. I come out in... well, itchy skin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.31,
      "end_seconds": 212.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.61,
      "end_seconds": 224.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.98,
      "text": "My partner and our baby. I work in accounts at a hospital. I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.87,
      "end_seconds": 229.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.13,
      "end_seconds": 233.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Erm, no, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.54,
      "end_seconds": 238.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.98,
      "end_seconds": 242.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "It's Tiotropium inhaler, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.6,
      "end_seconds": 246.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.4,
      "end_seconds": 249.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "I, I have COPD."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.49,
      "end_seconds": 260.47,
      "duration_seconds": 9.98,
      "text": "Sure. Let me tell you where I've got to. I think we're dealing with an ankle sprain without signs of a fracture at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.99,
      "end_seconds": 265.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Hmm, is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.88,
      "end_seconds": 293.97,
      "duration_seconds": 27.09,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with an ankle sprain without signs of a fracture do well once it's treated properly. I think an ankle X-ray makes sense here, for ankle injury. You'll be taking paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours if needed, for five days. It's for ankle pain. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.62,
      "end_seconds": 297.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.36,
      "end_seconds": 310.91,
      "duration_seconds": 12.55,
      "text": "Rest, ice, a firm bandage and keep it raised, and start gentle movement after two days. I'd like you to see physiotherapy as well, and I'll write the referral."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.63,
      "end_seconds": 313.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Alright, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.93,
      "end_seconds": 320.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again if it isn't better in a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.4,
      "end_seconds": 328.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Yeah, good, I'll return then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.47,
      "end_seconds": 334.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.09,
      "end_seconds": 341.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Hmm, um, I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.59,
      "end_seconds": 345.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}